3. Walking and oxygen model (plan B, labelled ESTIMATE on screen)
==========================================================================

Every walking and oxygen number in the app is labelled:
  "ESTIMATE: plan B over the relief, not the walking model yet"

Constants used (Assets/Walkback/App/ReturnStandIn.cs, HudEstimate.cs,
TerrainLayers.cs, ReturnFallback.cs):

  Slope pace           Tobler's hiking function, normalised to 1 on flat
                       ground. Function: Tobler, W. (1993), "Three
                       presentations on geographical analysis and
                       modeling", NCGIA Technical Report 93-1 (cited in
                       ReturnFallback.cs). Measured on Earth, without a
                       suit.
  Flat-ground pace     19.3 min/km. The code calls it the walking model's
                       own test number ("ficha A").
  Slope limit          20 degrees, no step on steeper ground.
  Oxygen walking       20 L of O2 per km on flat ground.
  Tank                 497 L of O2.
  Reserve              31 L (30 min), never touched.
  Design duration      480 min for the full tank (351 W design rate,
                       per the code comment).
  Task minutes         Proposed from NASA/TP-2017-219457, table 30 (see 1).

  Except Tobler's function and the task minutes, these constants come
  from the team's model notes ("ficha A"); their published sources are
  not written in this repository yet. They are the prototype's settings,
  not validated figures for a suited astronaut, and the app labels every
  number made with them ESTIMATE.


